	4. Protecting Data with Backups
		a. Comparing Backup types
			§ Backup utilities
				□ Protect from unexpected downtime
					® Malware infection, ransomware, server defacement
				□ Real-time file sync
					® rsync
				□ Regular partial backups - incremental, differential
				□ Complete coverage, fast recovery
			i. Full Backups
				§ Takes entire /whole backup
				§ Requires large amount of time and resources
				§ The most efficient way to restore the data
			ii. Restoring a Full Backup
				§ As it has whole backup, only one backup has to be applied.
				§ It takes the least amount of time to restore the backup
			iii. Differential Backups
				§ Takes backup till last full backup
				§ Time to take differential backup is between full backup and incremental backup 
				§ While restoring, it is more efficient than incremental but least efficient than full backup
				§ 
			iv. Order of Restoration for a Full/Differential Backup Set
				§ While system recovery, only 2 backups need to be applied ----> full backup and latest differential backup
			v. Incremental Backups
				§ Takes backup till last incremental backup or full backup
				§ Takes least amount of time while taking backup
				§ Takes most amount of time while restoring backup
			vi. Order or Restoration for a Full/Incremental Backup Set
				§ While system recovery, after applying full backup, all the incremental backups should be applied in chronological order they have taken.
			vii. Choosing Full/Incremental or Full/Differential'
				§ Should be chosen based on how much time can be allotted to taking backup and restoration.
				§ Differential will be better option when restoration should be faster
				§ Incremental should better option when you need time to take backup should be low.
			viii. Snapshot Backups
				§ Virtual systems, allows to take snapshot of the whole system and use it.
		b. Tape Rotation
			How long tape is going to be kept and when to replace it
			i. 10 tape rotation
				§ Each tape is used one per day for 2 weeks and then the entire set is reused.
			ii. Grandfather-Father-Son
				§ 3 sets of backup tapes are defined as the son(Daily), the father(weekly), and the grandfather(monthly)
			iii. Tower of Hanoi
				§ 3 sets of backup tapes (like grandfather-father-son) that are rotated in a more complex system
				§ 1st tape is used every 2nd day, 2nd tape used every 4th day, and 3rd tape is used every 8th day
		c. Testing Backups
			§ The phenomenon of testing the integrity and efficiency of backups.
			§ It ensures that backups taken actually works and all data can be recovered.
		d. Protecting Backups
