	5. Comparing Business Continuity Elements
		§ A Business impact analysis (BIA) is part of business continuity planning(BCP) and it identifies mission-essential functions, critical systems, and vulnerable business processes that are essential to the organization's success
		a. Business Impact Analysis Concepts (BIA)
			i. Impact
				§ The BIA identifies maximum downtimes for these systems and components, and the impact to life, property, safety, finance, and reputation form an incident
			ii. Privacy Impact and Threshold Assessments (PIA and PTA)
				§ Privacy threshold assessment (PTA) identifies if a system processes data that exceeds the threshold for PII.
				§ If the system processes PII, a privacy impact assessment helps identify and reduce risks related to potential loss of the PII.
			iii. Recovery Time Objective (RTO)
				§ It identifies the maximum amount of time it should take to restore a system after an outage.
			iv. Recovery Point Objective (RPO)
				§ It refers to the amount of data you can afford to lose.
			v. Comparing MTBF and MTTR
				§ Mean time between failures (MTBF) identifies the average time between failures
				§ Mean Time to recover identifies the average time it takes to restore a failed system.
		b. Continuity of Operations Planning (COOP)
			§ Continuity of operations planning identifies alternate processing sites and alternate business practices.
			i. Recovery Sites
				§ Recovery sites provide alternate locations for business functions after a major disaster.
				§ Hot site
					® Includes everything needed to be operational within 60 minutes.
					® It is most effective recovery solution and the most expensive
				§ Cold Site
					® It has power and connectivity requirements and little else.
					® It is the least expensive to maintain
				§ Warm Site
					® These are compromise between hot sites and cold sites,
			ii. Order of Restoration
				§ Based on the BIA, the mission critical services are to be brought up as soon as possible with maximum priority and then rest follows based on their priorities defined in BIA
